<title>USA: Ford 1996 North American exports rise.</title>
<headline>Ford 1996 North American exports rise.</headline>
<dateline>DEARBORN, Mich. 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ford Motor Co said Tuesday it shipped 139,528 cars and trucks in 1996 from plants in the U.S. and Canada, an increase of 35 percent from the 1995 total.</p>
<p>Ford said it exported 72,348 cars and 67,180 trucks. The top North American exported model was the Ranger compact pickup truck, followed by the Explorer sport/utility and Escort small car.</p>
<p>Ford ships vehicles to more than 120 countries. Top export markets are Brazil, Argentina, Japan, Puerto Rico, Chile and the Gulf Cooperation Council countries.</p>
</text>
